16r8|n|The longest, or longer, dimension of any object, in distinction from breadth or width; extent of anything from end to end; the longest line which can be drawn through a body, parallel to its sides; as, the length of a church, or of a ship; the length of a rope or line. ; A portion of space or of time considered as measured by its length; -- often in the plural. ; The quality or state of being long, in space or time; extent; duration; as, some sea birds are remarkable for the length of their wings; he was tired by the length of the sermon, and the length of his walk. ; A single piece or subdivision of a series, or of a number of long pieces which may be connected together; as, a length of pipe; a length of fence. ; Detail or amplification; unfolding; continuance as, to pursue a subject to a great length. ; Distance.	a:281j,58,3;1sh7,50,8;1av2,49,16;19jz,45,12;1gcs,43,9;19jm,41,9;24t4,41,6;2c1v,38,2;r9u,37,11;ucq,33,11;p8s,27,4;1w35,26,7;4no,25,1;263t,25,6;5ts,23,2~sem,13,18;1av2,49,16;19jz,45,12;r9u,37,11;ucq,33,11;19jm,41,9;1gcs,43,9;1sh7,50,8;1s8z,9,7;1w35,26,7;263t,25,6;24t4,41,6;1eah,1,6;bwc,18,4;p8s,27,4	v:dqp,49,3;788,8,1~dqp,49,3;788,8,1	V:1vkb,25,8~1vkb,25,8	n:1uwf,64,6;1rq5,59,73;4no,49,5;1sh7,48,7;2c1v,44,3;rch,37,24;8l2,27,3;a5p,27,3;23yz,26,3;263t,22,5;dnv,16,1;5ys,10,3;19jm,9,1;sem,9,14;rcd,3,5~1rq5,59,73;rch,37,24;sem,9,14;1bf4,1,7;1sh7,48,7;1uwf,64,6;263t,22,5;4no,49,5;rcd,3,5;2c1v,44,3;23yz,26,3;a5p,27,3;8l2,27,3;5ys,10,3;1wa7,2,2	N:1rl6,42,2;1rbt,40,8;178l,31,3;2bji,0,5~1rbt,40,8;2bji,0,5;178l,31,3;1rl6,42,2
