16uq|n|Anything read or recited to a teacher by a pupil or learner; something, as a portion of a book, assigned to a pupil to be studied or learned at one time. ; That which is learned or taught by an express effort; instruction derived from precept, experience, observation, or deduction; a precept; a doctrine; as, to take or give a lesson in drawing. ; A portion of Scripture read in divine service for instruction; as, here endeth the first lesson. ; A severe lecture; reproof; rebuke; warning. ; An exercise; a composition serving an educational purpose; a study.	a:28o4,67,3;111q,45,4~111q,45,4;28o4,67,3	V:16kf,78,6;1kol,66,1~16kf,78,6;1kol,66,1	N:16ki,79,1;1kol,66,1;1kn1,60,3~1kn1,60,3;1kol,66,1;16ki,79,1
